NAME
    hosts - static host name to IP mapping

DESCRIPTION
    /etc/hosts maps names to IPv4 addresses before any DNS traffic is
    sent, so entries work offline and always win over DNS answers.

    Each non-comment line lists an IP followed by one or more aliases:

        10.0.2.2    gateway
        10.0.2.15   vnu

    Lines starting with '#' are ignored; fields are separated by
    spaces or tabs. Lookups are case-insensitive. The file is seeded
    at boot and is a plain editable file (root: 0644).

FILES
    /etc/hosts
